//File:    recipes.jtext
//Date:    2026-10-30
//Purpose: Provision recipes (v001): the build prerequisites and, per OS family, the command that
//         installs each. bsir.sh runs these commands itself (one question, one sudo password);
//         jac313_test_cli setup names what is still missing.
//
// Data-driven, like compilers.jtext: to support a new OS, add its recipe_os rows, no code
// change. Readiness stays earned by sensing: after installing, bootstrap senses again, which
// refreshes FileCheckList.txt.
//
// components: one row per prerequisite.
//   component  its name; a compiler toolchain's recipe is named for the compilers.jtext label
//   desc       human description, shown as the heading while bootstrap installs it
//   for        toolchain label this provides: include when that REQUIRED toolchain is
//              missing per sensing (FileCheckList readiness). '' for standalone tools.
//   required   true = part of the readiness gate (earned by check)
//   check      shell test; exit 0 = already satisfied. Include the recipe when it FAILS.
//              '' = no check.
// recipe_os: one row per component per OS family.
//   os         OS family: rhel | fedora | linuxmint (FileCheckList's sensed os_family)
//   command    the install command on that OS family
//
// gcc15, gcc16, clang: the compiler toolchains (tied to compilers.jtext labels via for).
// sqlite: REQUIRED build dependency. Qlite links libsqlite3, so the dev headers must be
//   present BEFORE the build. Checked in bootstrap's baseline (bsir.sh) so bootstrap installs
//   it pre-build; without it `find_package(SQLite3)` fails on a fresh clone.
// pg18: REQUIRED for the Postgres persist sink and the PG local / PG remote gates: libpq 18+
//   client dev headers (PostgreSQL 18; the build needs libpq 18+). RHEL family: the PGDG
//   repo's postgresql18-devel (installs under /usr/pgsql-18; its perl-IPC-Run dependency
//   comes from CRB / CodeReady Builder, enabled here if missing). Fedora / Mint: the distro
//   or PGDG libpq dev package, version 18+.
// ninja: Ninja >= 1.11, required for C++23 module builds.
// cmake: the system package bootstraps the machine; the builds use the version in pinned_tools.
// vim: not needed by the build: an editor so a fresh machine has more than vi to fix files with.
// valgrind: REQUIRED prerequisite. memcheck + helgrind + DRD all ship INSIDE the one valgrind
//   package, so this single install covers the whole `matrix verify` / `verify-lite` gate.
//   Readiness is NOT READY without it (required = true: part of the readiness gate, earned by
//   check). The check requires BOTH the binary AND the dev header: the annotated verify tree
//   (-DJAC313_STORE_HELGRIND_ANNOTATE=ON) #includes <valgrind/helgrind.h>, which on
//   RHEL/Fedora ships in the SEPARATE valgrind-devel package (Debian bundles headers in
//   `valgrind`).
// upp_gui: the U++ GUI build (Jac313Runner / JTextGui). On purpose there is no check and no
//   for: only the bootstrap's GUI step uses it (skipped with --no-gui), after its own
//   pkg-config check. It installs GTK3 (U++'s Wayland-first GUI goes through GTK),
//   libnotify, FreeType, Fontconfig and the X11 libs that U++ CtrlCore links, and the MariaDB
//   client (JTextGui links libmariadb: mariadb-connector-c-devel, headers in /usr/include/mysql;
//   Mint libmariadb-dev, headers in /usr/include/mariadb). libpq comes from pg18, SQLite from
//   sqlite. U++ itself
//   comes from upp_basefix into UPP/<version>/install beside the repository (pinned GitHub commit + SHA-256-checked
//   tree, no sudo).
// dbeaver: the GUI step (skipped with --no-gui): DBeaver Community, a database browser for
//   results.db (SQLite) and the PostgreSQL / MariaDB tables. DBeaver's own package from its
//   GitHub release (Java included, about 130 MB), pinned to 26.2.3 with the sha256 GitHub
//   publishes. The Flathub Flatpak was 2.1 GB.
// chrome: the GUI step (skipped with --no-gui): Google Chrome, required by Jac313Runner's
//   "Open Reports in Chrome". Google's own repository, so dnf / apt check Google's
//   signature and keep Chrome updated. Google ships Chrome for Linux on x86_64 only.
//
// pinned_tools: a tool version an OS family must use. bsir.sh installs it into <tool>_install beside
//   the repository (no sudo), and the tool that runs it refuses any other version. No row = the
//   system's version.
//   valgrind: Mint's 3.22 reports false errors inside glibc's condition wait; 3.27.1 does not. Built
//   from source. The system valgrind package stays installed for its headers and libc6-dbg.
//   cmake: every system uses 4.3.0, so results do not depend on the distro's version (Mint's 3.28
//   does not even know cxx_std_26 for gcc, which v002 asks for). Kitware's x86_64 build, with the
//   sha256 Kitware publishes. A system cmake of exactly that version also passes; the package stays
//   installed either way.
//
// Formatter ^~ on the data rows (splice ^, comment ~): the commands hold |, ', &&, $(...),
// ; and {}, and bsir.sh reads this file with POSIX awk before anything is built. Keep one
// row per line and no comments on data rows.
//
=== jText File ===
 1. ?# recipes.jtext
 2. ?# 2026-10-30
 3. ?# Provision recipes: prerequisites and install commands by OS (v001)
